Ahui Hao is current a PhD candidate in the School of Materials Science and Engineering, Beihang University. Her research focuses on the design and fabrication of MOF-base materials in gas separation and energy conversion.
Prof. Jianglan Shui received one PhD degree from University of Science and Technology of China (2006) and one from University of Rochester (2010). He worked as a postdoctor at Argonne National Laboratory (2010–2013) and Case Western Reserve University (2013–2014). He joined School of Materials Science and Engineering at Beihang University in 2015. Prof. Shui's research focuses on key materials and devices for hydrogen energy, including electrocatalysts, hydrogen storage materials, and proton exchange membrane fuel cells.
